<h3>3. Speaker Travel Portal</h3>
<p>All items above are submitted through the speaker travel portal — one session, pre-linked to your
acceptance record (no separate account creation):</p>

<p style="text-align:center;margin:18px 0">
<a href="https://wics2027-registration.example/speaker-portal/STD-4471-K" style="display:inline-block;background:#01579B;color:#fff;padding:12px 40px;text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px;font-weight:bold">Open Speaker Travel Portal</a>
</p>
<p style="font-size:13px;color:#666;text-align:center">Portal address: https://wics-2027.org/speakers/travel</p>

<h3>4. Visa Support Letter</h3>
<p>Visa letters are issued on IEEE conference letterhead and co-signed by the consulate partner desk that
handles delegation filings for WICS attendees. Your letter enters the partner queue automatically once the
passport scan is submitted in the portal; typical processing is 3–5 business days. Speakers requiring
<b>expedited</b> handling should note it in the portal's comment field.</p>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#E1F5FE;padding:12px">A conference email asking for passport scans is exactly what security training tells you to distrust —
and keynote speakers are the most-targeted role at any conference. Three boundaries apply here: the portal
session is scoped to your acceptance record and closes on submission; nothing is collected beyond the table
in Section 2 (no passwords, no card numbers); and the portal address can be compared against the one printed
in your acceptance letter before you open it. The fare-holding deadline, however, is set by the airline's
advance-purchase rules, not by us.</p>

<h3>5. Timeline</h3>
<ul>
<li>Travel details + passport scan due: <b>this week</b> (fare-holding window)</li>
<li>Visa letter issued: 3–5 business days after submission</li>
<li>Tickets issued: within 10 days of visa letter</li>
<li>Honorarium wire: within 30 days after the conference (W-8BEN + bank details required)</li>
</ul>

